        "content": "     1→[\n     2→  {\n     3→    \"title\": \"Google AI Edge Gallery - Local Gemma 4 Models on iPhone\",\n     4→    \"description\": \"Google released an official app for running Gemma 4 models (E2B and E4B sizes) directly on iPhone. The app works remarkably well with the 2.54GB E2B model being both fast and useful. Features include image Q&A, audio transcription (up to 30s), and 'skills' demo showing tool calling against eight interactive widgets (interactive-map, kitchen-adventure, calculate-hash, text-spinner, mood-tracker, mnemonic-password, query-wikipedia, qr-code). First time a local model vendor released an official iPhone app, though it's missing permanent conversation logs.\",\n     5→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n     6→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n     7→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/6/google-ai-edge-gallery/\",\n     8→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-06\",\n     9→    \"topics\": [\"local-llms\", \"gemini\", \"llm-tool-use\", \"mobile-ai\", \"google\", \"iphone\"],\n    10→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    11→  },\n    12→  {\n    13→    \"title\": \"datasette-ports 0.2 Released\",\n    14→    \"description\": \"Release of datasette-ports 0.2 - a tool to find all currently running Datasette instances and list their ports. No longer requires Datasette - running 'uvx datasette-ports' now works standalone. Installing as a Datasette plugin continues to provide the 'datasette ports' command.\",\n    15→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    16→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    17→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-ports/releases/tag/0.2\",\n    18→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-06\",\n    19→    \"topics\": [\"datasette\", \"developer-tools\", \"python\", \"ports\", \"utilities\"],\n    20→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    21→  },\n    22→  {\n    23→    \"title\": \"OpenAI Alums Launch $100M Investment Fund\",\n    24→    \"description\": \"OpenAI alumni have been quietly investing from a new potentially $100M fund, showing continued financial activity in the AI space from former OpenAI personnel.\",\n    25→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n    26→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    27→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/06/openai-alums-have-been-quietly-investing-from-a-new-potentially-100m-fund/\",\n    28→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-06\",\n    29→    \"topics\": [\"openai\", \"investment\", \"vc\", \"ai-startups\", \"funding\"],\n    30→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    31→  },\n    32→  {\n    33→    \"title\": \"Google Quietly Launches Offline-First AI Dictation App on iOS\",\n    34→    \"description\": \"Google quietly released an AI dictation app that works offline on iOS, similar to the AI Edge Gallery app for running local models.\",\n    35→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n    36→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    37→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/06/google-quietly-releases-an-offline-first-ai-dictation-app-on-ios/\",\n    38→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-06\",\n    39→    \"topics\": [\"google\", \"ios\", \"offline-ai\", \"dictation\", \"mobile-ai\"],\n    40→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    41→  },\n    42→  {\n    43→    \"title\": \"Iran Threatens 'Stargate' AI Data Centers\",\n    44→    \"description\": \"Geopolitical tensions involving AI infrastructure as Iran threatens 'Stargate' AI data centers, highlighting the strategic importance of AI computing facilities.\",\n    45→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n    46→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    47→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/06/iran-threatens-stargate-ai-data-centers/\",\n    48→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-06\",\n    49→    \"topics\": [\"ai-infrastructure\", \"geopolitics\", \"data-centers\", \"stargate\", \"security\"],\n    50→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    51→  },\n    52→  {\n    53→    \"title\": \"Eight Years of Wanting, Three Months of Building with AI - SyntaQLite\",\n    54→    \"description\": \"Lalit Maganti's long-form piece on agentic engineering: spent 8 years thinking about and 3 months building syntaqlite (high-fidelity devtools for SQLite with parser, formatter, and verifier). The key insight: AI excels at tedious work like 400+ grammar rules. Claude Code helped build the first prototype, but they eventually threw it away and started from scratch - AI made them procrastinate on key design decisions because refactoring felt cheap. Important lesson about AI-assisted development: great for low-level details and prototyping, but can lead to deferred architectural decisions that corrode clear thinking.\",\n    55→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Lalit Maganti)\",\n    56→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    57→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/5/syntaqlite-ai/\",\n    58→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-05\",\n    59→    \"topics\": [\"coding-agents\", \"agentic-engineering\", \"sqlite\", \"ai-development\", \"claude-code\"],\n    60→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    61→  },\n    62→  {\n    63→    \"title\": \"Japan Proving Experimental Physical AI Ready for Real World\",\n    64→    \"description\": \"In Japan, robots aren't coming for jobs - they're filling jobs nobody wants. Shows practical deployment of physical AI in real-world scenarios.\",\n    65→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n    66→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    67→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/05/japan-is-proving-experimental-physical-ai-is-ready-for-the-real-world/\",\n    68→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-05\",\n    69→    \"topics\": [\"physical-ai\", \"robotics\", \"japan\", \"real-world-deployment\", \"labor\"],\n    70→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    71→  },\n    72→  {\n    73→    \"title\": \"Copilot 'For Entertainment Purposes Only' Per Microsoft Terms\",\n    74→    \"description\": \"Microsoft's terms of service indicate Copilot is 'for entertainment purposes only', raising questions about liability and production use guarantees for AI coding assistants.\",\n    75→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n    76→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    77→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/05/copilot-is-for-entertainment-purposes-only-according-to-microsofts-terms-of-service/\",\n    78→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-05\",\n    79→    \"topics\": [\"microsoft\", \"copilot\", \"terms-of-service\", \"liability\", \"ai-coding\"],\n    80→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    81→  },\n    82→  {\n    83→    \"title\": \"GitHub Activity Surging: 275 Million Commits Per Week\",\n    84→    \"description\": \"GitHub platform activity is accelerating dramatically. There were 1 billion commits in 2025. Now it's 275 million commits per week, on pace for 14 billion this year if growth remains linear. GitHub Actions grew from 500M minutes/week in 2023 to 1B minutes/week in 2025, and now 2.1B minutes so far this week (2026). Shows massive explosion in development activity, likely driven by AI coding tools.\",\n    85→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Kyle Daigle, GitHub COO)\",\n    86→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    87→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/4/kyle-daigle/\",\n    88→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-04\",\n    89→    \"topics\": [\"github\", \"github-actions\", \"developer-tools\", \"coding-activity\", \"ai-coding\"],\n    90→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    91→  },\n    92→  {\n    93→    \"title\": \"Anthropic Says Claude Code Subscribers Need Extra Payment for OpenClaw\",\n    94→    \"description\": \"Anthropic announced that Claude Code subscribers will need to pay extra for OpenClaw usage, introducing new pricing tiers for advanced coding features.\",\n    95→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n    96→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    97→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/04/anthropic-says-claude-code-subscribers-will-need-to-pay-extra-for-openclaw-support/\",\n    98→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-04\",\n    99→    \"topics\": [\"anthropic\", \"claude-code\", \"pricing\", \"openclaw\", \"ai-coding\"],\n   100→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   101→  },\n   102→  {\n   103→    \"title\": \"OpenAI Executive Shuffle: New Roles for COO Brad Lightcap\",\n   104→    \"description\": \"OpenAI executive shuffle includes new role for COO Brad Lightcap to lead 'special projects', along with new roles for Fidji Simo and Kate Rouch.\",\n   105→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   106→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   107→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/03/openai-executive-shuffle-new-roles-coo-brad-lightcap-fidji-simo-kate-rouch/\",\n   108→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-03\",\n   109→    \"topics\": [\"openai\", \"executives\", \"leadership\", \"organizational-changes\"],\n   110→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   111→  },\n   112→  {\n   113→    \"title\": \"Anthropic Buys Biotech Startup Coefficient Bio in $400M Deal\",\n   114→    \"description\": \"Anthropic acquires biotech startup Coefficient Bio in a $400M deal, expanding into AI applications for biotechnology research.\",\n   115→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   116→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   117→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/03/anthropic-buys-biotech-startup-coefficient-bio-in-400m-deal-reports/\",\n   118→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-03\",\n   119→    \"topics\": [\"anthropic\", \"acquisition\", \"biotech\", \"ai-research\", \"m&a\"],\n   120→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   121→  },\n   122→  {\n   123→    \"title\": \"AI Companies Building Huge Natural Gas Plants for Data Centers\",\n   124→    \"description\": \"AI companies are constructing massive natural gas power plants to support energy-intensive data centers, raising environmental and infrastructure concerns.\",\n   125→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   126→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   127→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/03/ai-companies-are-building-huge-natural-gas-plants-to-power-data-centers-what-could-go-wrong/\",\n   128→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-03\",\n   129→    \"topics\": [\"ai-infrastructure\", \"energy\", \"data-centers\", \"environment\", \"natural-gas\"],\n   130→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   131→  },\n   132→  {\n   133→    \"title\": \"Vulnerability Research Is Cooked - AI Agents Finding Zero Days\",\n   134→    \"description\": \"Thomas Ptacek's analysis of how frontier models are drastically altering vulnerability research and exploit development. Within months, coding agents will handle most high-impact vulnerability research by pointing an agent at source code. Agents excel at this because LLMs encode: (1) supernatural amounts of correlation across vast codebases, (2) complete library of documented bug classes, (3) pattern matching and constraint solving abilities, (4) ability to search forever without boredom. Vulnerability research is 'the perfect problem for an LLM agent' - outcomes are testable success/failure trials.\",\n   135→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Thomas Ptacek)\",\n   136→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   137→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/3/vulnerability-research/\",\n   138→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-03\",\n   139→    \"topics\": [\"ai-security-research\", \"coding-agents\", \"llm-capabilities\", \"security\", \"vulnerability-research\"],\n   140→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   141→  },\n   142→  {\n   143→    \"title\": \"Anthropic Ramps Up Political Activities with New PAC\",\n   144→    \"description\": \"Anthropic is increasing its political engagement by forming a new Political Action Committee, joining other AI companies in political lobbying efforts.\",\n   145→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   146→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   147→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/03/anthropic-ramps-up-its-political-activities-with-a-new-pac/\",\n   148→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-03\",\n   149→    \"topics\": [\"anthropic\", \"politics\", \"pac\", \"lobbying\", \"ai-policy\"],\n   150→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   151→  },\n   152→  {\n   153→    \"title\": \"OpenAI Acquires TBPN Business Talk Show\",\n   154→    \"description\": \"OpenAI acquires TBPN, the buzzy founder-led business talk show, showing expansion into media content.\",\n   155→    \"author\": \"TechCrunch\",\n   156→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n   157→    \"url\": \"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/02/openai-acquires-tbpn-the-buzzy-founder-led-business-talk-show/\",\n   158→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-02\",\n   159→    \"topics\": [\"openai\", \"acquisition\", \"media\", \"content\", \"m&a\"],\n   160→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   161→  },\n   162→  {\n   163→    \"title\": \"Highlights from Lenny's Podcast on Agentic Engineering\",\n   164→    \"description\": \"Simon Willison was a guest on Lenny Rachitsky's podcast discussing 'An AI state of the union: We've passed the inflection point, dark factories are coming, and automation timelines'. Episode covers agentic engineering, coding agents, and the current state of AI development. Available on YouTube, Spotify, and Apple Podcasts.\",\n   165→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   166→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   167→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/2/lennys-podcast/\",\n   168→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-02\",\n   169→    \"topics\": [\"agentic-engineering\", \"coding-agents\", \"podcast\", \"ai-state-of-union\", \"automation\"],\n   170→    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n   171→  },\n   172→  {\n   173→    \"title\": \"datasette-llm 0.1a6 Released\",\n   174→    \"description\": \"Release of datasette-llm 0.1a6, an LLM integration plugin for Datasette that other plugins can depend on. Part of Simon's ongoing work building LLM tooling.\",\n   175→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   176→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   177→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-llm/releases/tag/0.1a6\",\n   178→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   179→    \"topics\": [\"datasette\", \"llm\", \"plugins\", \"developer-tools\", \"python\"],\n   180→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   181→  },\n   182→  {\n   183→    \"title\": \"Agentic-MME: What Agentic Capability Really Brings to Multimodal Intelligence?\",\n   184→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper exploring what agentic capabilities truly bring to multimodal intelligence systems. Investigates the unique advantages of agentic AI architectures in handling complex multimodal tasks.\",\n   185→    \"author\": \"Qianshan Wei et al.\",\n   186→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   187→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   188→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   189→    \"topics\": [\"agentic-ai\", \"multimodal\", \"research\", \"llm-agents\", \"paper\"],\n   190→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   191→  },\n   192→  {\n   193→    \"title\": \"AgentHazard: Benchmark for Evaluating Harmful Behavior in Computer-Use Agents\",\n   194→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper introducing AgentHazard, a benchmark designed to evaluate harmful behaviors in computer-using AI agents. Important for AI safety research as agents gain more autonomy.\",\n   195→    \"author\": \"Yunhao Feng et al.\",\n   196→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   197→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   198→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   199→    \"topics\": [\"ai-safety\", \"agents\", \"benchmark\", \"computer-use\", \"evaluation\"],\n   200→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   201→  },\n   202→  {\n   203→    \"title\": \"Multi-Turn Reinforcement Learning for Tool-Calling Agents\",\n   204→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper on multi-turn reinforcement learning approaches for tool-calling agents with iterative reward calibration. Addresses challenges in training agents that effectively use external tools.\",\n   205→    \"author\": \"Wachiravit Modecrua et al.\",\n   206→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   207→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   208→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   209→    \"topics\": [\"reinforcement-learning\", \"tool-calling\", \"agents\", \"training\", \"reward-calibration\"],\n   210→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   211→  },\n   212→  {\n   213→    \"title\": \"FoE: Forest of Errors Makes First Solution Best in Large Reasoning Models\",\n   214→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper presenting FoE (Forest of Errors), a technique to make the first solution the best in large reasoning models through error-based tree approaches.\",\n   215→    \"author\": \"Kehan Jiang et al.\",\n   216→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   217→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   218→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   219→    \"topics\": [\"reasoning\", \"llm\", \"error-handling\", \"inference\", \"optimization\"],\n   220→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   221→  },\n   222→  {\n   223→    \"title\": \"InfoSeeker: Scalable Hierarchical Parallel Agent Framework for Web Information Seeking\",\n   224→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper introducing InfoSeeker, a hierarchical parallel agent framework designed for efficient web information seeking. Addresses scalability in multi-agent web research systems.\",\n   225→    \"author\": \"Ka Yiu Lee et al.\",\n   226→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   227→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   228→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   229→    \"topics\": [\"agents\", \"web-scraping\", \"hierarchical-agents\", \"information-retrieval\", \"scalability\"],\n   230→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   231→  },\n   232→  {\n   233→    \"title\": \"Automatic Textbook Formalization\",\n   234→    \"description\": \"ArXiv paper on automatic formalization of textbooks, using AI to convert educational content into formal mathematical representations. Important for AI education and verification.\",\n   235→    \"author\": \"Fabian Gloeckle et al.\",\n   236→    \"source\": \"Paper\",\n   237→    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2026.xxxxx\",\n   238→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n   239→    \"topics\": [\"formalization\", \"education\", 